lowing{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-05-08T21:48:49Z","updated_at":"2024-05-08T21:49:55Z","body":"Probably - something @stellaraccident may have a pointer to/thoughts about - I'm not sure what the right solution is at that level. We can't do much in IREE as the only safe behavior is to silently insert copies for any externally-provided buffer and that defeats the purpose of the in-place ops. I'm not sure if analysis at the torch level could insert the copies, warn/error if they're required, or what :/\r\n\r\n(this is one of the reasons we default to not doing in-place operations - they've got footguns :)","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/2101537617/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/2101639008","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/17316#issuecomment-2101639008","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/17316","id":2101639008,"node_id":"IC_kwDODGgK6M59RHdg","user":{"login":"stellaraccident","id":494208,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NDIwOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/494208?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellaraccident","html_url":"https://github.com/stellaraccident","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellaraccident/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellaraccident/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellaraccident/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellaraccident/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellaraccident/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellaraccident/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellaraccident/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellaraccident/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellaraccident/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-05-08T23:05:14Z","updated_at":"2024-05-08T23:05:14Z","body":"I think my eyes aren't calibrated right to see where this is becoming a move-like thing. Probably need some help figuring out how to structure it.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/2101639008/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/2101650326","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/17316#issuecomment-2101650326","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/17316","id":2101650326,"node_id":"IC_kwDODGgK6M59RKOW","user":{"login":"benvanik","id":75337,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MzM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75337?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik","html_url":"https://github.com/benvanik","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-05-08T23:18:37Z","updated_at":"2024-05-08T23:18:37Z","body":"I don't know torch stuff (vtensor? what?), but maybe it's whatever to_vtensor is?\r\nindex_put ties operand 0 to its result so %0 is %2, assuming to_vtensor is not a forced copy %0 is %arg0, and the final overwrite aliases %2 to %arg0. so %arg0 == %0 == %2.\r\n\r\nIf to_vtensor must remain a clone and doesn't end up as a flow.tensor.clone then the above will happen. Even if it does become a clone maybe we're dropping it later and that's something we could fix locally but will be trickier in more complex programs to prove. A print-after-all would be useful.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/2101650326/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/2101696083","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/17316#issuecomment-2101696083","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/17316","id":2101696083,"node_id":"IC_kwDODGgK6M59RVZT","user":{"login":"stellaraccident","id":494208,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NDIwOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/494208?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellaraccident","html_url":"https://github.com/stellaraccident","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellaraccident/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellaraccident/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellaraccident/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellaraccident/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellaraccident/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellaraccident/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellaraccident/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellaraccident/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellaraccident/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-05-09T00:11:05Z","updated_at":"2024-05-09T00:11:05Z","body":"Chatting with Ben, the repro is not strictly legal (it is returning a value that is in-placed). While we could support that form, it is presently a limitation. Also, I think it is a testing artifact. We should work on this case:\r\n\r\n```\r\nmodule @module {\r\n  func.func @test_index_copy(%arg0: !torch.tensor<[8192,16,8,128],f32>, %arg1: !torch.vtensor<[4],si64>, %arg2: !torch.vtensor<[4,16,8,128],f32>) {\r\n    %0 = torch.copy.to_vtensor %arg0 : !torch.vtensor<[8192,16,8,128],f32>\r\n    %1 = torch.prim.ListConstruct %arg1 : (!torch.vtensor<[4],si64>) -> !torch.list<optional<vtensor>>\r\n    %false = torch.constant.bool false\r\n    %2 = torch.aten.index_put %0, %1, %arg2, %false : !torch.vtensor<[8192,16,8,128],f32>, !torch.list<optional<vtensor>>, !torch.vtensor<[4,16,8,128],f32>, !torch.bool -> !torch.vtensor<[8192,16,8,128],f32>\r\n    torch.overwrite.tensor.contents %2 overwrites %arg0 : !torch.vtensor<[8192,16,8,128],f32>, !torch.tensor<[8192,16,8,128],f32>\r\n    return\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/2101696083/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/2101732607","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/17316#issuecomment-2101732607","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/17316","id":2101732607,"node_id":"IC_kwDODGgK6M59ReT_","user":{"login":"benvanik","id":75337,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MzM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75337?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik","html_url":"https://github.com/benvanik","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-05-09T00:54:26Z","updated_at":"2024-05-09T00:54:26Z","body":"notes to tomorrow me:\r\n- remove into from hal.tensor.export\r\n- add a hal.tensor.alias (or whatever) op: `%tied = hal.tensor.alias %operand, %storage : tensor<..>, !hal.buffer_view -> %operand`\r\n- change torch stuff to use that, drop optimization_barrier and hal.tensor.export\r\n- ensure emplace allocations uses the alias\r\n- error checking if two logical tensors (through tied ops) have an alias defined","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/2101732607/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0